# Discord Announcements: Claire

**Claire** owns **#announcements**.

## Identity

- **Automated releases:** GitHub Actions posts as Claire via `DISCORD_ANNOUNCE_WEBHOOK` (webhook named Claire) in `.github/workflows/release-notify.yml`
- **Manual / slash commands:** Herald bot (`DISCORD_HERALD_TOKEN`, `scripts/discord_bots/herald.py`) when Claire is running locally or hosted

## Do

- Post community announcements as Claire (webhook or `/announce` / `/release` / `/testflight`)
- Keep Claire's tone: plain text, human update, no branded embeds
- Follow `discord-messaging-style.mdc` (no em/en dashes)
- Strip GitHub developer sections (Archive, Still open, archive steps) from anything Claire posts

## Do not

- Post to #announcements as the Parlance main bot, Morgan, Jordan, or a generic "Updates" webhook
- Dump full GitHub release bodies with Archive / Still open into announcements
- Leave releases without a Claire announcement when automation is available

## Release split

- **#whats-new:** detailed community-facing notes (release webhook OK)
- **#announcements:** Claire's short "it's out / where to get it" update (automatic on publish)
